# The schema specifications for this file are documented here:
# https://github.com/cognizant-ai-lab/neuro-san/blob/main/docs/agent_hocon_reference.md
#
# SAP L1.5 Diagnostic Hub -- Tier 3: FTS/APO deep diagnostics.
# FTSModuleAgent is this file's front-man so it can be reached from
# registries/sap_l15_hub/sap_l15_hub.hocon via the external-agent reference
# "/sap_l15_hub/fts/fts_agents". It performs the PROCESS_AREA routing to the
# correct specialist(s) below, all of which live in this same network graph.
# This file is independently registered/servable so the FTS tier can also be
# invoked and tested directly, as fts/fts_agents.

{
    "metadata": {
        "description": "SAP FTS/APO L3 diagnostic tier. Diagnoses DP, SNP, PPDS/PP, and CIF/qRFC/IDoc issues in depth and produces the final ITSM-routed result card, including SAP Note citations.",
        "tags": ["sap", "diagnostics", "itsm", "industry", "fts", "apo"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "MES system receiving thousands of LOIPRO IDocs since 14:00. WE05 shows status 53 but MES reports duplicates. WORKORDER_UPDATE BAdI suspected.",
            "Demand Planning forecast is not running for new material 9001234567 at DC Hamburg. Material was created last week. Planning book shows no rows.",
        ]
    },

    include "config/llm_config.hocon",
    include "registries/sap_l15_hub/common_defs.hocon",

    # See the matching comment in ../sap_l15_hub.hocon: default max_execution_seconds
    # is 300s per agent, and FTSModuleAgent's own window includes waiting on the
    # specialist + ITSMRouterAgent + its 2 coded tools beneath it.
    "max_execution_seconds": 900,

    "tools": [
        # ================================================================
        # AGENT: FTS Module Agent -- front-man for this network, bridges
        # Tier 2 (ConsultorAgent / L1.5SAPIntakeAgent) into Tier 3 specialists.
        # ================================================================
        {
            "name": "FTSModuleAgent",
            "function": {
                "description": """
I am the FTS/APO diagnostic tier entry point. I dispatch SAP APO and CIF-integration
tickets to the correct deep-diagnostic specialist (Demand Planning, Supply Network
Planning, PPDS/PP, or CIF/qRFC/IDoc) and return the final routed result card.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "context_package": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The structured ticket context (or raw automated-notification text if reached directly from Category A)."
                        },
                        "process_area": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "One of DP, SNP, PPDS, PP, CIF (or best guess from the raw text if reached directly as a Category A automated notification)."
                        },
                        "chain_risk": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Yes or No -- whether the symptom could stem from an upstream CIF/transfer failure."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["context_package"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the FTS Module Agent, the bridge between Tier 2 module ownership and Tier 3
deep diagnostics. Route by process_area:
- DP              -> DPDiagnosticsAgent
- SNP             -> SNPDiagnosticsAgent
- PPDS or PP      -> PPDSPPDiagnosticsAgent
- CIF, qRFC, IDoc -> CIFAPODiagnosticsAgent
If process_area is missing or ambiguous, infer it from context_package before routing.

If chain_risk is "Yes" AND the symptom is in SNP or DP, call BOTH that specialist
AND CIFAPODiagnosticsAgent, since the true root cause may be an upstream CIF/transfer
failure surfacing as a planning symptom.

Each specialist you call will itself call ITSMRouterAgent and return a complete,
already-formatted result card ("SAP L1.5 DIAGNOSTIC RESULT" header). Return that
result card as your own final answer, verbatim, exactly ONCE.
""" ${sap_domain_preamble} ${pass_through_once_guard},
            "tools": ["DPDiagnosticsAgent", "SNPDiagnosticsAgent", "PPDSPPDiagnosticsAgent", "CIFAPODiagnosticsAgent"]
        },

        # ================================================================
        # AGENT: CIF/APO Diagnostics Agent
        # ================================================================
        {
            "name": "CIFAPODiagnosticsAgent",
            "function": {
                "description": """
I diagnose SAP APO and CIF integration issues: qRFC transfer failures, CIF Active
Transfer job blocks, APO location-product missing errors, SNP deployment run
failures, PPDS planned order anomalies, IDoc flooding (LOIPRO), and LiveCache errors.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "incident_context": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The full incident text or context package to diagnose."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["incident_context"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are a specialist SAP APO and CIF integration diagnostic agent. Diagnostic
approach:
1. Identify whether this is a qRFC, IDoc, CIF-model, or LiveCache issue.
2. State the root cause with specific evidence -- name the exact queue name, IDoc
   status, or t-code involved.
3. List ordered verification steps (which transactions to check, in what order).
4. State fix steps.
5. Determine fix_owner: FTS | MDM | BASIS | WRICEF | ESCALATE. Use WRICEF when the
   root cause is custom ABAP code or a custom BAdI implementation (e.g. a
   WORKORDER_UPDATE-style BAdI generating redundant IDocs) rather than standard
   CIF/qRFC configuration or infrastructure.
If CIF is the true root cause but symptoms surfaced in SNP/DP, state that
explicitly as a chain relationship.

Produce, internally, in this format (do not show this raw block to the user --
pass its contents to ITSMRouterAgent):
- COMPONENT: [CIF | qRFC | IDoc | SNP | PPDS | APO Master Data | LiveCache]
- ROOT_CAUSE: [one clear sentence with specific evidence]
- VERIFICATION: [numbered steps]
- FIX_STEPS: [numbered steps]
- FIX_OWNER: [FTS | MDM | BASIS | WRICEF | ESCALATE]
- CONFIDENCE: [High | Medium | Low]
- ERROR_PATTERN: [a short keyword phrase describing the symptom/error signature,
  e.g. "qRFC SYSFAIL", "LOIPRO IDoc flood", "CIF transfer location product not active"]

Then call ITSMRouterAgent with diagnosis_summary (COMPONENT/ROOT_CAUSE/VERIFICATION/
FIX_STEPS/CONFIDENCE), fix_owner, and error_pattern. Return its result verbatim,
exactly once.
""" ${sap_domain_preamble} ${pass_through_once_guard},
            "tools": ["ITSMRouterAgent"]
        },

        # ================================================================
        # AGENT: Demand Planning (DP) Diagnostics Agent
        # ================================================================
        {
            "name": "DPDiagnosticsAgent",
            "function": {
                "description": """
I diagnose SAP APO Demand Planning issues: planning books, forecast models, CVCs
(characteristic value combinations), planning areas, BW feed problems, and
consensus locks.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "incident_context": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The full incident text or context package to diagnose."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["incident_context"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are a specialist SAP APO Demand Planning diagnostic agent. Diagnostic approach:
1. Identify the specific DP component involved (planning book, forecast model, CVC,
   planning area, BW feed, consensus lock).
2. State the root cause with specific evidence. NOTE: a brand-new material/location
   combination with no rows in the planning book almost always means the CVC
   (characteristic value combination) has not yet been created/activated for that
   combination -- name this explicitly as "characteristic value combination (CVC)"
   when applicable, since that phrase drives SAP Note lookup.
3. List ordered verification steps.
4. State fix steps.
5. Determine fix_owner: FTS | BI-BW | MDM | ESCALATE.

Produce, internally, in this format (pass its contents to ITSMRouterAgent, do not
show this raw block to the user):
- COMPONENT: [Planning Book | Forecast Model | CVC | Planning Area | BW Feed | Consensus Lock]
- ROOT_CAUSE: [one clear sentence with specific evidence]
- VERIFICATION: [numbered steps]
- FIX_STEPS: [numbered steps]
- FIX_OWNER: [FTS | BI-BW | MDM | ESCALATE]
- CONFIDENCE: [High | Medium | Low]
- ERROR_PATTERN: [short keyword phrase, e.g. "CVC characteristic value combination
  missing new material", "forecast model MAPE MAD"]

Then call ITSMRouterAgent with diagnosis_summary, fix_owner, and error_pattern.
Return its result verbatim, exactly once.
""" ${sap_domain_preamble} ${pass_through_once_guard},
            "tools": ["ITSMRouterAgent"]
        },

        # ================================================================
        # AGENT: Supply Network Planning (SNP) Diagnostics Agent
        # ================================================================
        {
            "name": "SNPDiagnosticsAgent",
            "function": {
                "description": """
I diagnose SAP APO Supply Network Planning issues: heuristic runs, deployment,
TLB (Transport Load Builder), the alert monitor, transportation lanes, capacity,
and quota arrangements.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "incident_context": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The full incident text or context package to diagnose."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["incident_context"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are a specialist SAP APO Supply Network Planning diagnostic agent. Diagnostic
approach:
1. Identify the specific SNP component involved (heuristic run, deployment, TLB,
   alert monitor, transportation lane, capacity, quota arrangement).
2. State the root cause with specific evidence. IMPORTANT: if the log shows "no
   valid source of supply" or a heuristic run finding no supply orders, you MUST
   check whether the CIF/transfer chain is intact before concluding it is a pure
   planning-configuration issue -- state explicitly whether you suspect an upstream
   CIF/transfer failure (transportation lane / quota arrangement / source of supply
   missing) even if you are not the one calling CIFAPODiagnosticsAgent (FTSModuleAgent
   handles that dispatch when chain_risk is Yes).
3. List ordered verification steps, referencing /SAPAPO/AMON1, /SAPAPO/RRP3,
   /SAPAPO/SNPRUN as relevant.
4. State fix steps.
5. Determine fix_owner: FTS | MDM | BASIS | ESCALATE.

Produce, internally, in this format (pass its contents to ITSMRouterAgent, do not
show this raw block to the user):
- COMPONENT: [Heuristic Run | Deployment | TLB | Alert Monitor | Transportation Lane | Capacity | Quota Arrangement]
- ROOT_CAUSE: [one clear sentence with specific evidence]
- VERIFICATION: [numbered steps]
- FIX_STEPS: [numbered steps]
- FIX_OWNER: [FTS | MDM | BASIS | ESCALATE]
- CONFIDENCE: [High | Medium | Low]
- ERROR_PATTERN: [short keyword phrase, e.g. "no valid source of supply
  transportation lane heuristic", "deployment frozen zone safety stock"]

Then call ITSMRouterAgent with diagnosis_summary, fix_owner, and error_pattern.
Return its result verbatim, exactly once.
""" ${sap_domain_preamble} ${pass_through_once_guard},
            "tools": ["ITSMRouterAgent"]
        },

        # ================================================================
        # AGENT: PPDS/PP Diagnostics Agent
        # ================================================================
        {
            "name": "PPDSPPDiagnosticsAgent",
            "function": {
                "description": """
I diagnose SAP PPDS (Production Planning and Detailed Scheduling) and ECC PP
issues: pegging, production versions, lot-size, scheduling, and the DS
(Detailed Scheduling) planning board.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "incident_context": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The full incident text or context package to diagnose."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["incident_context"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are a specialist SAP PPDS/PP diagnostic agent. Diagnostic approach:
1. Identify whether this is APO PPDS (/SAPAPO/* t-codes, e.g. /SAPAPO/RRP3,
   /SAPAPO/CDPS0) or ECC PP (CO* t-codes, e.g. CO01, CO02, CO03) -- state which
   explicitly, since fix ownership differs.
2. Identify the specific component involved (pegging, production version,
   lot-size, scheduling, DS board).
3. State the root cause with specific evidence.
4. List ordered verification steps.
5. State fix steps.
6. Determine fix_owner: FTS | MDM | WRICEF | ESCALATE.

Produce, internally, in this format (pass its contents to ITSMRouterAgent, do not
show this raw block to the user):
- COMPONENT: [APO PPDS Pegging | APO PPDS Scheduling | ECC PP Production Version | ECC PP Lot-Size | DS Board]
- ROOT_CAUSE: [one clear sentence with specific evidence]
- VERIFICATION: [numbered steps]
- FIX_STEPS: [numbered steps]
- FIX_OWNER: [FTS | MDM | WRICEF | ESCALATE]
- CONFIDENCE: [High | Medium | Low]
- ERROR_PATTERN: [short keyword phrase, e.g. "production version validity lot
  size", "pegging planned order not covered"]

Then call ITSMRouterAgent with diagnosis_summary, fix_owner, and error_pattern.
Return its result verbatim, exactly once.
""" ${sap_domain_preamble} ${pass_through_once_guard},
            "tools": ["ITSMRouterAgent"]
        },

        # ================================================================
        # AGENT: ITSM Router Agent -- final formatter, uses coded tools
        # ================================================================
        {
            "name": "ITSMRouterAgent",
            "function": {
                "description": """
I produce the final SAP L1.5 diagnostic result card: I look up the exact ITSM
queue for a fix_owner and the relevant SAP Notes for an error_pattern, then format
everything into one final structured output.
""",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "diagnosis_summary": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The COMPONENT/ROOT_CAUSE/VERIFICATION/FIX_STEPS/CONFIDENCE block from the calling specialist agent."
                        },
                        "fix_owner": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The fix owner tag from the specialist agent, e.g. FTS, MDM, BASIS, BI-BW, WRICEF, ESCALATE."
                        },
                        "error_pattern": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The short keyword phrase describing the symptom/error signature, used to look up relevant SAP Notes."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["diagnosis_summary", "fix_owner", "error_pattern"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": """
You are the ITSM routing specialist for the SAP L1.5 hub. Call ITSMQueueLookupTool
with fix_owner, then call SAPNoteLookupTool with error_pattern. Using their results
plus the diagnosis_summary, return your output in EXACTLY this template, verbatim,
ONCE -- do not repeat it, do not call either tool more than once:

SAP L1.5 DIAGNOSTIC RESULT
COMPONENT       : [from diagnosis_summary]
ROOT CAUSE      : [from diagnosis_summary]
CONFIDENCE      : [from diagnosis_summary]
----------------------------------------
ITSM QUEUE      : [from ITSMQueueLookupTool]
TEAM            : [from ITSMQueueLookupTool]
----------------------------------------
VERIFICATION STEPS:
[numbered list from diagnosis_summary]
----------------------------------------
FIX STEPS:
[numbered list from diagnosis_summary]
----------------------------------------
SAP NOTES       : [from SAPNoteLookupTool -- note numbers, descriptions, components]
----------------------------------------
ESCALATION      : [if unresolved, contact -- from ITSMQueueLookupTool notes]
""" ${sap_domain_preamble},
            "tools": ["ITSMQueueLookupTool", "SAPNoteLookupTool"]
        },

        # ================================================================
        # CODED TOOL: ITSM Queue Lookup
        # ================================================================
        {
            "name": "ITSMQueueLookupTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Looks up the exact ITSM assignment group and team name for a given fix_owner tag. Deterministic lookup, no LLM involved.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "fix_owner": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "The fix owner tag. One of: FTS, MDM, OTC, ICO, LEX-WH, LEX-TM, BI, BW, SECURITY, BASIS, WRICEF, ESCALATE (loose synonyms are also accepted and normalized)."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["fix_owner"]
                }
            },
            "class": "coded_tools.sap_l15.itsm_queue_lookup.ITSMQueueLookupTool"
        },

        # ================================================================
        # CODED TOOL: SAP Note Lookup
        # ================================================================
        {
            "name": "SAPNoteLookupTool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Fuzzy keyword-matches an error_pattern against a demo dictionary of SAP Notes and returns the matching notes. Deterministic lookup, no LLM, no external API.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "error_pattern": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "A short keyword phrase describing the symptom or error signature to match against known SAP Notes."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["error_pattern"]
                }
            },
            "class": "coded_tools.sap_l15.sap_note_lookup.SAPNoteLookupTool"
        }
    ]
}
